      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting, the C code checks this using a mix signed/unsigned logic:\n\n```\n\tif (host_id \u003e\u003d motion_sensor_count)\n\t\treturn NULL;\n\tsensor \u003d \u0026motion_sensors[host_id];\n\t\t\n```\n\nThe assembly shows that a signed comparison is used:\n```\n        if (host_id \u003e\u003d motion_sensor_count)\n10086ed4:       2804            cmp     r0, #4\n10086ed6:       dc10            bgt.n   10086efa \u003chost_sensor_id_to_real_sensor+0x26\u003e\n                return NULL;\n```\n\n\"bgt\" is the signed version of branch if greater than. \"bhs\" is the unsigned version - branch higher or same.\n\nThis appears to work because the host command interface the packs the sensor number into a `uint8_t`, so -1 gets converted to 0xFF, which is safely below `INT_MAX` and is interpreted as +255.\n\nI\u0027d recommend using `UINT8_MAX` after changing the parameters types on `host_cmd_motion_sense_info()`.",
